  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice.\r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan, dated 07/08/2026\rExisting and Proposed Block Plan, ref: EP001, dated 06/08/2026\rProposed Floor Plans (Ground Floor and First Floor), ref: P001, dated 06/08/2026\rProposed Floor Plans (Loft Floor and Roof Plan), ref: P002, dated 06/08/2026\rProposed Front and Rear Elevation, ref: P003, dated 06/08/2026\rProposed Side Elevations, ref: P004, dated 06/08/2026\rProposed Section (Section AA), ref: P005, dated 06/08/2026\rSite Plan, ref: SP001, dated 06/08/2026\rBins and Bikes Storage Details, ref: SP002, dated 06/08/2026\rPlanning Statement, dated August 2026\rHighway Safety Impact Assessment Proforma\rMinor SuDS Profoma\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dining room at ground floor and secondary kitchen at the top floor shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in C4 Use.\r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accommodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.",
    "Prior to occupation, the cycle parking facilities as shown on the approved drawings shall be implemented in full and shall thereafter be retained.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of secure and adequate cycle parking.",
    "Prior to occupation of the HMO hereby approved, details of waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy that the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and to ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials."
  ]
